    {
      "duration_ms": 11000,
      "caption": "Per-vCPU state lives in the VMCS: guest state, host state, controls, exit info.",
      "narration": "Each vCPU has a VMCS, made current with VMPTRLD and edited with VMWRITE. It holds guest and host state, execution controls, and read-only exit information fields.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "The VMCS",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "v",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Guest-state area (RIP, CR3, ...)",
            "Host-state area (reload on exit)",
            "VM-execution / entry / exit controls",
            "Exit info: EXIT_REASON, QUALIFICATION"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20.0,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "color": "purple"
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "VMXON, VMCLEAR, VMPTRLD, VMWRITE",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 62.4,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 1900,
          "enter": "fade",
          "color": "gray"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 11000,
      "caption": "The hypervisor loops: enter guest, exit, read EXIT_REASON, emulate, resume.",
      "narration": "The core is a loop. Enter with VMLAUNCH the first time, VMRESUME afterwards. On exit, read the reason, emulate the instruction, advance guest RIP, and resume.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "The run loop",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "loop",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "VMPTRLD vmcs\nVMLAUNCH   (later: VMRESUME)\n... guest runs ...\nexit: read EXIT_REASON\nemulate, advance guest RIP",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20.0,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "hl-loop",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "loop",
          "at": 2300
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 11000,
      "caption": "KVM dispatches on exit reason through a handler table in vmx.c.",
      "narration": "In KVM, vmx_vcpu_run does the entry. After an exit, vmx_handle_exit indexes kvm_vmx_exit_handlers by exit reason, such as CPUID, I/O or an EPT violation.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Exit reasons in KVM",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "tbl",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "c",
          "text": "[EXIT_REASON_CPUID] = kvm_emulate_cpuid,\n[EXIT_REASON_IO_INSTRUCTION] = handle_io,\n[EXIT_REASON_EPT_VIOLATION] = handle_ept_violation,",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20.0,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "f",
